# Working research notes. A private record, never committed. Unanchored on
# purpose: a NOTES/ at any depth is private.
NOTES/

# Third-party originals and solver output. Anchored with a leading slash, so
# `docs/data/` and any other directory called `data` further down is tracked.
/data/*
/outputs/

# The converted reference data is the exception. It is small, it is derived by
# our own scripts or copied unchanged from a dataset we published (the PREM
# profiles from Zenodo), and every plot, score and test depends on it, so
# tracking it means the site builds and the tests run with no network and with
# no permission to re-host anyone else's files.
!/data/converted/

# The GIAMIP organisers' shared folder, as a browser downloads it. Its files are
# repacked into data/original/giamip/, so the download itself is never tracked.
/GIAMIP Official Protocol-*.zip

# Quarto build products. `_freeze/` is the execution cache that a local render
# writes. It is not committed: CI executes every page on each render, and no
# page reads the third-party originals.
/_site/
/.quarto/
/_freeze/

# Quarto writes a `.quarto_ipynb` file beside each page while it executes the
# page. It adds this pattern to .gitignore when the pattern is absent, so the
# pattern is here to keep a local render from changing this file.
**/*.quarto_ipynb

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/

# macOS
.DS_Store
